                    <mxGeometry x="260" y="168" width="70" height="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="112" value="Depth 3" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="400" y="168" width="70" height="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="114" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;" parent="1" source="113" target="109" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="113" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;In the input_x_y/output_x_y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;x stands for the depth of the node/output&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;y stands for the local Id of the node&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="150" y="483" width="240" height="60" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="116" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;" parent="1" source="115" target="109" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="115" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;To implement :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;- A way to assign local id&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;- A surcharge of the __add methods&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;to accept list&amp;lt;str&amp;gt; inputs&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;- A graph traversal algorithm that sort&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;the nodes according to their depth&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Advantages :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;- Easy to organize and to decrypt :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;depth parser algorithm&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;- We keep all the functionalities and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;basically the same organization, only&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;the input is changed to a list of input&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;- As we keep the same organization,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;it&#39;s coherent with the code and easy to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;modify.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Inconvenient :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;- The internal representation need to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;go through an adapter to add the depth&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;and local Id, I don&#39;t know if the current&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;architecture is easily modulable, if not,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;the surcharge of the __add methods might&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;be harder than expected and more complicated&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;- To identify the nodes depth, we need a graph&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;traversal algorithm that outputs an list of depth&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;and within each depth there&#39;ll be the nodes id&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;(I already know how to do one). Depending on&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;the NN Structures, it might be time consuming&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;(And on top of that we use Python soo...)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;- As already said, this implementation requires&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;a surcharg of the add function, that means we have&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;double the already existing codes, that&#39;ll take a lot of&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;space and time although it shouldn&#39;t be difficult.&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="-130" y="710" width="300" height="520" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>